{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791057627,"nonce":"GbJUIal02RggyWI6NbTzLvz8mmU=","message":"Plan for CSS stylesheets (port of Blinc's blinc_css, standard CSS plus pointer queries, no @flow), agreed 2026-10-03.\n\nDepartures from Blinc, on purpose:\n- A per-property cascade by specificity then source order. Blinc replaces a whole ElementStyle for a repeated #id rule and on merge.\n- Layering as decided: stylesheet rules \u003c Tw utilities \u003c style= \u003c attributes. Blinc applies CSS over builder values. This needs an unset in blinc_abi's property router, to drop a value when its rule stops matching.\n- Matching on change, not per frame: elements are matched when attached (at flush, as Relations resolves group-/peer-), and re-matched when their classes, the tree around them, a stylesheet or a state their rules read changes. Only elements whose rules use :hover etc. subscribe to Interaction.\n- var() follows the theme reactively, rather than re-parsing all CSS on a scheme change.\n- Pointer queries on any rule, not only #id ones, with pointer-space parent/viewport implemented (Blinc parses them and ignores them).\n\nElement CSS classes (user's choice): one class= in hxx. Words Tw knows are utilities; the rest are CSS classes, checked at compile time against the .css files the build declares (-D ashui_css=...). CSS added only at run time can match any class, but unknown names in hxx are compile errors.\n\nStages, each committed and tested:\n1. Parser (Haxe, run time and macro time): grammar, selectors (type, #id, .class, *, descendant \u003e + ~, states, structural pseudo-classes, :not/:is/:where/:has, ::placeholder), :root variables, @keyframes, diagnostics with line and column. Blinc's parser tests ported.\n2. Value parsers: colours (adding hsl and the full named-colour list), lengths and units, calc(), gradients, shadows, transforms, filters, clip paths (reusing ClipPathCss).\n3. Element identity: id, CSS classes, element type, from hxx and Haxe.\n4. Matching, cascade and layering, with the router unset.\n5. States: :hover, :active, :focus, :focus-visible, :disabled, through Interaction.\n6. Theme variables, reactive (ThemeState's CSS variable map).\n7. transition and @keyframes on ashui.animation.\n8. Pointer queries and env().\n9. Loading: Stylesheet.parse(text), files, CSS with a theme bundle, and reloading a saved .css file in development.","files":null}]}